FEATURES             Location/Qualifiers
     rep_origin      1..223
                     /label="pSC101 ori (SpeI-free BioBrick form)"
                     /synonym="pSC101 ori (pSB4 form)"
                     /synonym="pSC101 ori (BioBrick form)"
                     /note="The SpeI-free BioBrick form of the pSC101 origin:
                     the native origin with two changes (T22A, A23T) that remove
                     the ACTAGT SpeI site at its bases 20-25. The iGEM Registry
                     record of the pSC101 origin (BBa_I50042) describes it as
                     carrying ""mutations introduced to eliminate a SpeI site""
                     and as ""the origin of replication in pSB4* series
                     plasmids""; the pSB4A5 backbone carries the same 223 bp.
                     That record calls the origin ""supposed to have low copy
                     number"", and the pSB4A5 record gives the plasmid's copy
                     number as ~10-12 (citing Lutz & Bujard 1997). Copy-number
                     mutations of pSC101 map in the rep101 gene, not in the
                     origin (Armstrong et al. 1984); no source checked here ties
                     a copy-number phenotype to these two bases, and none ties a
                     temperature sensitivity to any form of this origin."
                     /db_xref="SO:0000296"
                     /citation=[4]
                     /citation=[5]
                     /variant_of="pSC101 ori"
